-- title:
--   Descent of σ-stable quasi-compact opens to Spec B
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime and let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi$ an irreducible element of $\mathcal O$, $\mathcal O$ assumed $\pi$-adically complete, with residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ of cardinality $r$ and with $(r)=(\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$ (absolute unramifiedness). Let $\mathrm{Onr}$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, $\mathrm{Fr}$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism of $\mathrm{Onr}$, and assume: $\mathrm{Onr}$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $\mathrm{Onr}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo it, every monic polynomial over $\mathrm{Onr}$ of positive degree has a root modulo it, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo it for all $x$. Let $m>0$, let $S=\{x\in\mathrm{Onr}:\mathrm{Fr}^{m}(x)=x\}$ be the equalizer of $\mathrm{Fr}^{m}$ and the identity, and let $\mathrm{FrS}$ be an $S$-algebra automorphism of $\mathrm{Onr}$ with $\mathrm{FrS}(x)=\mathrm{Fr}^{m}(x)$ for all $x$. Let $B$ be a commutative ring which is both an $\mathcal O$-algebra and an $S$-algebra, compatibly, with the image of $\pi$ in $B$ nilpotent. Let $U$ be an open subscheme of $\operatorname{Spec}(B\otimes_{S}\mathrm{Onr})$ whose underlying set is quasi-compact and which satisfies $\sigma^{-1}(U)=U$, where $\sigma=\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{id}_{B}\otimes\mathrm{FrS}$. Then there is an open $V\subseteq\operatorname{Spec} B$ with quasi-compact underlying set whose preimage under the morphism induced by $b\mapsto b\otimes 1$ is exactly $U$.
--
--   This is the topological half of Čerednik–Drinfeld-style descent along the unramified base change $S\to\mathrm{Onr}$: a quasi-compact open of $\operatorname{Spec}(B\otimes_S\mathrm{Onr})$ invariant under the Frobenius $\sigma$ comes from $\operatorname{Spec} B$. It rests on the description of the Teichmüller levels $\{x:\mathrm{Fr}^{mk}x=x\}$ and on the corresponding affine descent statement for elements, and is used in turn to descend morphisms of schemes that commute with $\sigma$.
